SECTION K. PROFIT AND COMMISSION RULES (BUILD A REAL, TESTED CALCULATOR)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------
Build the math as a small PURE function in one file (profitEngine) so it is easy to test. Use whole cents (integers) to avoid rounding mistakes.

Example (all numbers come from Settings / the agreement snapshot):
- New Trader deposits $100. Total profit = $100.
- New Trader share 80% = $80.
- Professional Trader share 20% = $20.
- Platform commission 2% of TOTAL profit = $2, taken OUT OF the Professional Trader's share.
- Professional Trader gets $20 - $2 = $18.
- Final split: New Trader 80% / Professional Trader 18% / Shohoj Trading 2%.

Rules:
- The New Trader's deposit is never shared. Only eligible profit is shared.
- Commission is calculated on total profit but paid from the Professional Trader's share. The New Trader is never charged extra.
- The three final shares must add up to exactly 100%. Show a visible check. If it fails, show an error and block saving.
- Block any setting where commission is bigger than the Professional Trader's share.
- Use realized net profit (closed trades only), not floating profit.
- Use a HIGH-WATER MARK: fee only on new profit, not on money that only recovers old losses.
- Deposits and withdrawals during the period are NOT counted as profit or loss.
- Trading costs (spread, swap, commission) are included in net profit.
- If there is a loss, no profit fee is charged. The loss is carried forward under the high-water mark.
- Add a "Profit Calculator" playground page where anyone can try numbers and see the split step by step.
- Add a small "Self-test" panel in Demo Tools that runs 8 or more test cases on the engine (profit, loss, recovery, deposit in the middle, withdrawal in the middle, different split, 100% check, rounding) and shows pass or fail.

